      },
      "worked": "For $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, the reciprocal functions are defined and $1-\\cos\\theta\\ne0$. Multiply the inner numerator and denominator by $\\sin\\theta$, then rationalise.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\cot\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}}\\\\\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\cot\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{(1+\\cos\\theta)(1-\\cos\\theta)}{(1-\\cos\\theta)^2}}\\\\\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\cot\\theta}}&=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{(1-\\cos\\theta)^2}}\\\\\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-\\cot\\theta}}&=\\left|\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1-\\cos\\theta}\\right|.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe final step uses $\\sqrt{a^2}=|a|$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
